   "html_text": "A number of luck egalitarian accounts suggest that how much talent people have is a matter of luck, whereas their levels of effort are not. Metaphorically speaking, the first is a matter of the cards one has been dealt, whereas the latter is a matter of how one chooses to play them. To be sure, it will often be plausible to say that one’s present level of talent reflects past effort, and that one’s level of effort is a matter of good or bad luck (Rawls 1971, 74). Partly for the sake of simplicit",
